{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-250933",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{10}=-224$ and ${a}_{5}=7.$ Substituting $n=10$ and $m=5$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{10-5} & =\\frac{{a}_{10}}{{a}_{5}} \\\\ {r}^{5} & =\\frac{(-224)}{7} \\\\ {r}^{5} & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{5} & =-32 \\\\ {r}^{5} & =(-2)^{5} \\\\ r & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
